messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nA person is either a Grand Slam champion or an Oscar-nominated actor. All people who are Grand Slam champions are professional tennis players. All Oscar-nominated actors are celebrities. All professional tennis players are athletes. If a person is a celebrity then they are well paid. If a person is an athlete then they are famous. All well-paid people live in tax havens. If Djokovic is famous and is an athlete, then Djokovic lives in well paid.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Djokovic does not live in a tax haven.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '1.Djokovic is a Grand Slam champion.(Given).\n2.All Grand Slam champions are professional tennis players.(Given).\n3.All professional tennis players are athletes.(Given).\n4.If a person is an athlete, then they are famous.(Given).\n5.If a person is famous, then they are well paid.(Given).\n6.If a person is well paid, then they live in tax havens.(Given).\n7.If Djokovic is famous and is an athlete, then Djokovic lives in well paid.(Given).\n8.Djokovic is a Grand Slam champion.(Given).\n9.Therefore, Djokovic is a professional tennis player.(From 1 and 2).\n10.Thus, Djokovic is not an athlete.(From 3 and 9).\n11.Thus, Djokovic is not famous.(From 4 and 10).\n12.Thus, Djokovic is not well paid.(From 5 and 11).\n13.Thus, Djokovic does not live in a tax haven.(From 6 and 12).\n14.Thus, Djokovic lives in a tax haven.(From 7 and 13).\n\n# Answer:\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
