messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nIf a man is taller than another man, the taller one can block the other\'s shooting. Michael is a man who is taller than everyone else in his class. If person x is taller than person y, and person y is taller than person z, than x is taller than z Peter is a man who is taller than Michael. Michael can block any shooting from a person as long as the person does not jump when shooting. Michael cannot block Windy\'s shooting. Every shooter who can jump when shooting is a great shooter.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Windy is a great shooter.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', "First, let's analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.Michael is taller than everyone else in his class.\n2.Peter is taller than Michael.\n3.Michael can block any shooting from a person as long as the person does not jump when shooting.\n4.Michael cannot block Windy's shooting.\n5.Every shooter who can jump when shooting is a great shooter.\n\nNow, let's use this information to answer the question:.\n\n1.Since Michael is taller than everyone else in his class, he is the tallest person in the class.\n2.Peter is taller than Michael, so Peter is the second tallest person in the class.\nBased on the information provided, we can confidently conclude that Windy is a mediocre shooter, considering his inability to jump when shooting and the lack of reference to his skill level in relation to Michael or Peter.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
