messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAll aliens are extraterrestrial. If someone is from Mars, then they are aliens. No extraterrestrial is human. Everyone from Earth is a human. Marvin cannot be from Earth and from Mars. If Marvin is not from Earth, then Marvin is an extraterrestrial.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Marvin is neither a human nor from Mars.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '1.All aliens are extraterrestrial.(Given).\n2.If someone is from Mars, then they are aliens.(Given).\n3.No extraterrestrial is human.(Given).\n4.Everyone from Earth is a human.(Given).\n5.Marvin cannot be from Earth and from Mars.(Given).\n6.If Marvin is not from Earth, then Marvin is an extraterrestrial.(Given).\n\n## Step-by-Step Reasoning:.\n1.From step 1, we know that all aliens are extraterrestrial.\n2.From step 2, if someone is from Mars, then they are aliens.\n3.From step 3, no extraterrestrial is human.Since all aliens are extraterrestrial (step 1), Marvin is not an alien. Therefore, Marvin is either a human or from Mars.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
