messages:   36%|###5      | 73/204 [01:16<04:42,  2.15s/it][['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAll people who have a wedding are people who have at least one child. All people who travel to Paris for their honeymoon are people who have a wedding. All weddings that occur in July belong to people who travel to Paris for their honeymoon. Some weddings in July are well-attended. If John has at least one child, then John does not travel to Paris for his honeymoon and does not have a wedding. If John has a wedding that is well-attended, then John has a wedding in July or, if not, then John travels to Paris for their honeymoon.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? John has neither a wedding that is well-attended nor does he travel to Paris for his honeymoon.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '1.John has at least one child.(Given).\n2.All people who have a wedding are people who have at least one child.(Given).\n3.Therefore, John has a wedding.(From 1 and 2).\n4.All weddings that occur in July belong to people who travel to Paris for their honeymoon.(Given).\n5.All people who travel to Paris for their honeymoon are people who have a wedding.(Given).\n6.Therefore, John travels to Paris for his honeymoon.(From 4 and 5).\n7.If John has a wedding that is well-attended, then John has a wedding in July or, if not, then John travels to Paris for their honeymoon.(Given).\n8.John has a wedding that is well-attended.(From 3).\n9.Therefore, John does not have a wedding in July.(From 7 and 8).\n10.John travels to Paris for his honeymoon.(From 6).\n11.John has a wedding.(From 10).\n12.John has a wedding that is well-attended and he travels to Paris for his honeymoon.(From 11).\n\n# Answer:\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
