messages:   70%|######9   | 142/204 [03:23<01:09,  1.12s/it][['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock does not have wings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', 'First, let\'s analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.All mammals are animals.\n2.All monkeys are mammals.\n3.An animal is either a monkey or a bird.\n4.All birds fly.\n5.All animals breathe.\n6.If something can fly, then it has wings.\n7.If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\nNow, let\'s examine the statement "Rock does not have wings.".\n\nFrom point 1, we know that all mammals are animals.Since Rock is neither a fly nor a bird (point 6), it cannot be a bird.Therefore, Rock must be an animal.\n\nFrom point 2, we know that all monkeys are mammals.Since Rock is an animal, it could be a monkey.However, we don\'t have enough information to determine if Rock is a monkey or not.\n\nFrom point 3, we know that an animal is either a monkey or a bird.Since Rock is neither a fly nor a bird (point 6), it cannot be a bird.Therefore, Rock must have wings.\n\nFrom point 4, we know that all birds fly.Since Rock is a monkey (point 3), it can fly.\n\nFrom point 5, we know that all animals breathe.Since Rock is an animal (point 1), it must not breathe.\n\nFrom point 6, we know that if Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.Since Rock is a monkey (point 3) and can fly (point 4), it flies.\n\nFrom point 7, we know that if Rock can fly, then it has wings.Since Rock can fly (point 6), it has wings.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Rock does not have wings" is false.\n\n# Answer:\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
