her their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school.\n6.Bonnie either both attends and is very engaged with school events and is a student who attends the school, or she neither attends and is very engaged with school events nor is a student who attends the school.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement:.\n\n"If Bonnie either chaperones high school dances or, if she does not, she performs in school talent shows often, then Bonnie is both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and an inactive and disinterested member of the community.".\n\nTo determine if this statement is true, false, or uncertain, we need to consider the following:.\n\n1.If Bonnie chaperones high school dances, then she is not a student who attends the school (from point 3).\nIf Bonnie neither chaperones high school dances nor performs in school talent shows often, then she is neither a young child nor teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities nor an inactive and disinterested member of the community.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
