om home.".\n\nTo determine if the statement is true, false, or uncertain, we need to consider the possible scenarios for James:.\n\n1.James is a manager and appears in the company today.\n2.James is not a manager and appears in the company today.\n3.James is a manager and does not appear in the company today.\n4.James is not a manager and does not appear in the company today.\n\nLet\'s analyze each scenario:.\n\n1.If James is a manager and appears in the company today, then he must have lunch in the company (from point 2).Since he is a manager, he cannot work remotely from home (from point 6).Therefore, James must have lunch at home (from point 4).This scenario satisfies the statement.Since none of the scenarios satisfy the statement, the statement is false.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
